{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VY9BGPHWL53YH5jGHaeeye","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## File Contents Summary\n\nI have successfully read all three files. Here's the complete contents:\n\n---\n\n### 1. docs/specs/software-requirements/srd083-truncate.yaml\n\n**Full requirements specification for the truncate command:**\n\n**R1: Size specification**\n- R1.1: `-s SIZE` or `--size=SIZE` sets file size to SIZE bytes with unit suffixes (K, M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y for powers of 1024; KB, MB, GB for powers of 1000)\n- R1.2: SIZE can be prefixed with `+` (grow), `-` (shrink), `<` (at most), `>` (at least), `/` (round down), `%` (round up)\n- R1.3: Multiple FILE arguments apply the same operation to each\n- R1.4: `-c` or `--no-create` prevents creating missing files; without it, missing files are created\n\n**R2: Reference file**\n- R2.1: `-r RFILE` or `--reference=RFILE` uses RFILE's size as base, can combine with `-s` for relative adjustment\n- R2.2: Exit 1 if reference file cannot be accessed\n\n**R3: Exit codes and SIGPIPE** (focus area)\n- R3.1: Exit 0 when all files processed successfully\n- R3.2: Exit 1 when any file cannot be opened/created/resized or SIZE is invalid\n- R3.3: Handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler`\n\nThe spec also includes 5 acceptance criteria (AC1-AC5) covering basic operations, differential testing against `gtruncate`, and linting requirements.\n\n---\n\n### 2. cmd/truncate/main.go\n\n**Complete implementation (364 lines):**\n\nThe implementation includes:\n- Help and version text constants\n- Options struct with fields: `noCreate`, `ioBlocks`, `reference`, `sizeStr`, `sizeSet`\n- `main()` function that installs SIGPIPE handler, parses arguments, validates required options, and calls `run()`\n- `run()` function that processes reference file (if specified), parses size modifier/value, and truncates each file\n- `truncateFile()` function that ensures file exists (or skips if `-c`), computes new size, and calls `os.Truncate()`\n- `ensureFile()` function that stats the file, creates it if missing and not `-c`, returns FileInfo\n- `computeSize()` function that handles base size calculation with reference or current size\n- `applySize()` function that applies modifiers (+, -, <, >, /, %) to sizes\n- `parseSize()` function that extracts modifier and numeric value from SIZE string\n- `parseArgs()` function that handles `--`, long flags, and short flags\n- `parseLongFlag()` and `parseShortFlags()` functions for option parsing\n- `ioBlockSize()` helper that gets filesystem block size via syscall.Statfs\n- Utility functions: `quote()`, `errMsg()`, `capitalizeFirst()`\n\nKey imports: `os`, `syscall`, `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sizeparse`, `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n\n---\n\n### 3. cmd/truncate/truncate_test.go\n\n**Complete test file (260 lines):**\n\nContains:\n- Helper functions: `normalizeBinaryName()` and `normalizeErrors()` for output normalization\n- `TestDiff()` function that runs differential tests against `gtruncate` reference binary\n  - Builds the Go binary and looks up `gtruncate`\n  - 29+ test cases covering:\n    - Absolute sizes (0, 100, 200)\n    - Unit suffixes (K, KB)\n    - Multiple files\n    - `-c/--no-create` flag\n    - Missing reference file\n    - Error cases (missing operands, invalid sizes)\n    - Relative adjustments (+50, -20)\n    - Comparisons (<, >)\n    - Rounding (/, %)\n    - Reference file operations (with and without relative size)\n- `TestNoCreateSkipsCreation()` function that verifies `-c` flag prevents file creation\n\nTests use `testutils.DiffTest` with `testutils.RunDiffTests()` for differential testing against `gtruncate`.\n\n---\n\nAll three files work together to implement a complete truncate utility with comprehensive requirement coverage (R1-R3) and extensive test coverage matching GNU coreutils behavior."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"s